  "conclusions": [
    "The observed base-to-current degradation is broad: unaffected blocks and ordinary/pre-join targets also have higher loss. It is not concentrated in missing-EOS boundaries.",
    "Ordinary/pre-join targets increase by about 0.03947 loss and post-join context targets by about 0.03924, nearly the same magnitude.",
    "The 226 immediate boundary targets become easier (loss 18.4744 to 15.7039). Their tiny weight makes a negative contribution of about -0.000299, slightly offsetting the total increase.",
    "Fully unaffected regular blocks increase by about 0.04158, more than the about 0.03055 increase in blocks containing missing-EOS joins.",
    "Quota truncation is a real validation representativeness/packing issue, but these measurements do not support it as the main explanation of the observed base-to-current loss increase."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This compares the pinned base with the retained current checkpoint at step 181650. The discarded step-5000 minimum checkpoint was not evaluated, so this cannot directly decompose the minimum-to-current increase.",
    "Partition contributions are arithmetic descriptions on this fixed validation set, not causal interventions. Ordinary/pre-join targets combine all unaffected blocks with prefixes of affected blocks.",
    "The original HF scalar loss uses FP32 aggregation; stratified sums use FP64. Their delta differs by about 2.5e-7 and is within the specified 1e-6 tolerance.",
    "Marginal_groups contains two overlapping classifications. Reconstruct pilot+extension and missing+regular separately; summing all four marginals would double-count the full set."
  ],
